   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Before, I tied that, I know that",
   "texto": [
    "**Antes que** (before), **até que** (until) and **sem que** (without which) usually go with conjunctive for an unrealized action: **Antes que saias, fecha a porta** (before you leave, close the door), **Até que chegues** (until you arrive). The subject may be the same or different."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Before + infinitive",
   "texto": [
    "With **antes de**, the infinitive can be left without bending when the subject is understood by the context: **Antes de sair, vou fechar a porta** (before leaving, I will close the door). If the subject of the subordinate is expressed or should be identified, it can be flexed: **Antes de saíres, vou fechar a porta** (before you leave, I will close the door).",
    "**Saíres** is an infinitive pessoal «tu»; it is not a conjunctive."
   ]
  },
